{"title":"Minimum Window Substring","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"Given two strings s and t of lengths m and n respectively, return the minimum window substring of s such that every character in t (including duplicates) is included in the window. If there is no such substring, return the empty string \"\".\nThe testcases will be generated such that the minimum window is unique. If equal-length windows nevertheless occur, return the one with the smallest starting index.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t = \"ABC\"\nOutput: \"BANC\"\n```\n\nThe minimum window substring \"BANC\" includes 'A', 'B', and 'C' from string t.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"a\", t = \"a\"\nOutput: \"a\"\n```\n\nThe entire string s is the minimum window.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: s = \"a\", t = \"aa\"\nOutput: \"\"\n```\n\nBoth 'a's from t must be included in the window.\nSince the largest window of s only has one 'a', return empty string.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- m == s.length\n- n == t.length\n- 1 <= m, n <= 10^5\n- s and t consist of uppercase and lowercase English letters.\n","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def minWindow(self, s: str, t: str) -> str:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().minWindow","parameters":[{"name":"s","type":"str"},{"name":"t","type":"str"}],"returnType":"str","tests":[{"input":["A","A"],"expected":"A"},{"input":["A","aBAzzBzAaABz"],"expected":""},{"input":["A","zA"],"expected":""},{"input":["AA","AA"],"expected":"AA"},{"input":[{"$json":"eJztwbEAAAAAAjCXTPKXSqNjWwoAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAADcygD7LTSy","bytes":100002},"B"],"expected":""},{"input":[{"$json":"eJztwTEBAAAMAqAuNtH+oVZjB5ACAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAXy0H+y80sw==","bytes":100002},{"$json":"eJztwTEBAAAMAqAuNtH+oVZjB5ACAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA